==English==
{{wp|+ (mathematics)}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷem-}}
{{etymon|en|:af|eventual|-ly<id:adverbial>|text=+|tree=1}} The third sense is influenced by any of several European languages, including {{cog|cs|eventuálně}}, {{cog|fr|éventuellement}}, {{cog|sv|eventuellt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈvɛn.t͡ʃuː.ə.li/|/ɪˈvɛn.t͡ʃʊ.li/|/ɪˈvɛn.tjʊ.li/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈvɛn.t͡ʃu.ə.li/|/ɪˈvɛn.t͡ʃu.li/|/ɪˈvɛn.t͡ʃə.li/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-eventually.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{U|in the end}}; at some later time, especially after a long time, a series of problems, struggles, delays or setbacks.
#: {{ux|en|Everyone's [[show one's true colors|true colors]] will be revealed '''eventually'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|She didn't arrive.  '''Eventually''', we started without her.}}
#: {{ux|en|He hopes '''eventually''' to attend nursing school.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author={{w|Chris Wallace (journalist)|Chris Wallace}}|title=Character: Profiles in Presidential Courage|passage=It had taken nine years from the evening that Truman first showed up with a pie plate at her mother's door, but his dogged perseverance '''eventually''' won him the hand of his boyhood Sunday school crush.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Nick Paton Walsh|title=Trump’s second term could bring chaos around the world. Will it work?|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/09/world/analysis-trump-second-term-world-intl/index.html|date=2024-11-09|passage=President Volodymyr Zelensky has known the day would come when the idea of another “forever war” became unappealing to NATO, and the world’s largest military alliance '''eventually''' sought to wind down its involvement.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250817181423/https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/09/world/analysis-trump-second-term-world-intl/index.html|archivedate=17 August 2025}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|of a sequence}} For some [[tail]]; for all terms beyond some term; with only finitely many exceptions.
#: {{ux|en|'''Eventually''', all prime numbers are odd.}}
# {{lb|en|proscribed|NNSE}} {{U|possibly}}, [[potentially]], [[perhaps]].
#: {{ux|en|I will come '''eventually''', but haven't decided yet.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{lb|en|sense|in the end}} {{l|en|at last}}, {{l|en|finally}}, {{l|en|yet}}, {{l|en|ultimately}}, {{l|en|in the end}}

